---
description: Cursor runtime routing for EGM workflows only.
alwaysApply: true
---

Apply these instructions only to an EGM workflow.
Before execution, identify the absolute path of the selected EGM SKILL.md.
For EGM_ROOT/skills/<directory>/SKILL.md, ascend three directories to EGM_ROOT.
Confirm that EGM_ROOT/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json,
EGM_ROOT/agents/, EGM_ROOT/resources/, and EGM_ROOT/docs/cursor.md exist.
If the skill path is unavailable, ask for the installed package's absolute path.
Read EGM_ROOT/docs/cursor.md before following the canonical skill.
Do not infer a cache location or use another installed EGM version.

Resolve agents/, resources/, and docs/ against EGM_ROOT. Resolve references/
against the invoked skill directory. Pass absolute file paths to each child.
This path mapping does not depend on variable substitution in Markdown.

Keep drafting, synthesis, remediation, and report writes in the parent.
Use direct Task dispatch to the registered EGM reviewer types.
Start a new task for every independent reviewer. Never resume a reviewer.
Supply EGM_ROOT, the target and scope, persona and standard paths, and only
the explicit Goldfish context. Do not include parent history or deliberation.
Do not pass earlier findings except where the canonical workflow requires them.
Do not dispatch the canonical synthesizer or bootstrap orchestrator as a
generic child. Their native adapters are not included in this experiment.

Wait for every reviewer completion before advancing the stage.
Write each completed stage report before dispatching the next stage.
For Step 8, pass the absolute path of the existing zoom_out_report.md to the
reviewer. If the report is missing, stop the review.
Keep the canonical stage order and human approval gates.
If a reviewer cannot start, read required files, or finish, stop the stage.
Report the incomplete review. Do not simulate a reviewer in the parent.
Missing host evidence leaves isolation unverified, even if findings exist.
